# Shell scripts must keep LF endings on every platform.
#
# internal/monitor/pcapd.sh is embedded with //go:embed and shipped to a RHEL host
# as base64; a single CR would break its shebang and every line of it. The launch
# path normalises endings defensively, but with core.autocrlf=true a Windows clone
# would still check the file out as CRLF and fail TestPcapdNoCRLF, so pin it here.
*.sh text eol=lf
